    "result_text": "All tests pass (39/39, BUILD SUCCESS), including the changed checkpoints and the full suite.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated the three separate owner duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) into a single derived `identityKey`.\n\n**`identityKey` = `normalizedTelephone` + `|` + (email or empty) + `|` + (householdId or empty)** \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone, the stored lower-cased email, and the household id. A create is rejected with **409 only when a new owner's whole `identityKey` exactly equals an existing owner's**.\n\n### Key design point\nBecause `householdId` is part of the key and is assigned/back-filled *during* creation, the single check runs **after** `build` and `assignHousehold`, so the new owner's key (and every existing member's key) is finalized before comparison. This makes two members of the same household with **different telephones** produce different keys \u2014 both allowed \u2014 while an exact full-key match collides. On a 409 the pipeline transaction rolls back any household back-fill.\n\n### Changes\n- **New pipeline order** (`owners.POST.yml`): `validate \u2192 build \u2192 assignHousehold \u2192 checkIdentityUnique \u2192 checkCityCapacity \u2192 checkDailyLimit \u2192 \u2026`. The duplicate check still precedes the capacity/limit checks, preserving the original \"duplicate rejected first\" precedence.\n- **`OwnerIdentity`** (util) \u2014 single source of truth for `key(Owner)`, reused by both the check and the response mapper.\n- **`CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`** \u2014 the one consolidated check, throwing new checked **`DuplicateIdentityException`** (\u2192 409 via handler + escalation YAML).\n- **`OwnerMapper`** + **openapi.yml** \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` field so it's returned on the owner response (verified by Cp11's `telephone||householdId` assertion).\n- **Removed** the three obsolete `CheckOwner*Unique` classes and the `DuplicateTelephone/Email/Household` exceptions, handlers, and escalation YAMLs.\n\nBehaviour tests confirming this: full duplicates collide (Cp03/Cp10/Cp25/Cp28), household members with distinct telephones coexist and share a `householdId` (Cp11/Cp23).",
